{
  "opening": "This release introduces several key features and bug fixes to enhance type safety, validation flexibility, and error handling. We are adding support for Python 3.12, updating default behaviors for schema ordering, and refining the URL and DateTime fields.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m37",
      "text": "The library must expose an Enum field capable of handling enumeration types. The public API must include the names EnumSymbol, EnumValue, IPv6Interface, and Method."
    },
    {
      "id": "m42",
      "text": "The library must provide a unified Enum field that replaces separate EnumSymbol and EnumValue implementations. The public API must include the names Enum, EnumSymbol, EnumValue, and IPv6Interface."
    },
    {
      "id": "m53",
      "text": "The DateTime field must support loading and dumping dates using timestamp formats, including millisecond precision. The public API must expose the names AwareDateTime, DateTime, NaiveDateTime, from_iso_date, from_timestamp, from_timestamp_ms, isoformat, timestamp, and timestamp_ms."
    },
    {
      "id": "m109",
      "text": "The URL validator and Url field must accept an absolute parameter to control whether relative URLs are permitted during validation. The public API must include the names URL and Url."
    },
    {
      "id": "m112",
      "text": "The from_timestamp utility function must handle OSError and OverflowError exceptions gracefully instead of raising unhandled errors. The public API must include the name from_timestamp."
    },
    {
      "id": "m118",
      "text": "Nested partial schemas must correctly inherit their parent schema's partial setting by default. The public API must include the name Schema."
    },
    {
      "id": "m119",
      "text": "Schemas must use OrderedSet as the default set_class, ensuring that fields are ordered by default. The public API must include the names Field, Meta, Schema, SchemaMeta, UserSchema, and set_class."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names listed in the requirements are exposed exactly as specified. These changes align with our goal of providing robust serialization tools for modern Python applications."
}
